			<div class="content" id="post-content-4312270">
									

<p>I haven't read your prior drafts, but I don't think this submission is helped by the interview logs or the journal.</p>
<p>At the start, it's a creepy ring and two subjects who are connected to it in an interesting way, and I want to learn more. But all of the addenda just tell a bog-standard domestic abuse story, nothing even anomalous about them. There aren't any compelling developments to the story either: I'd guessed what the final journal entries would be as soon as I read the first one.</p>
<p>I think <strong>all</strong> the backstory needs to be implied, rather than outward stated. Having SCP-4168-2 make one or two statements is fine, but don't dedicate any paragraphs to it. Find a way to tell only the bare essentials of the story, and let the audience make conclusions.</p>

							</div>

								
					
