			<div class="content" id="post-content-4313713">
									

<div style="text-align: justify;">
<p>I cannot bring myself to downvote the article, seeing how much the author is trying to improve it. Yet I cannot really upvote it right now.</p>
<p>The formatting in the diary section is weird - the words don't stay on the lines and are sometimes crossed by the lines.</p>
<p>I enjoy the story. I enjoy the more human side of the Foundation - they cannot separate the abuser and his victim physically but they can at least put the abuser in the coma for some time. (I mean, they could possibly put him in a coma for a longer time..) And I feel really sorry for the victim, what the abuser did is horrible.</p>
<p>However, I don't think that the diary adds anything to the article (although it highlights the victim's personality a bit, so maybe it is just formatting that puts me off). And the last interview - that is a bit extra too. While it gives the reader a confirmation that the abuser is who he is, it is a bit unnecessary - almost everyone would have put 2 and 2 together by that point. So the last interview feels like the author holds my hand a bit too tight. Yet, it made me dislike the abuser a bit more.</p>
<p>Novote for now, but I would definitely upvote when the formatting is a bit better.</p>
<p>Edit: I've changed my mind - the article grew on me. +1</p>
</div>

