				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/lilac-snow" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(5210371); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=5210371&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1608238215" alt="Lilac Snow" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=5210371)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/lilac-snow" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(5210371); return false;" >Lilac Snow</a></span> <span class="odate time_1565852619 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">15 Aug 2019 07:03</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4331128">
									

<p>My thoughts on this are generally similar to many others’: I love the idea itself, but certain things about the article put me off a bit.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;show&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>For starters, a lot of the sentences seem awkward, like they need commas. “Dr.” should have a space after it before the name, and there are too many ellipses at one part. The dialogue in general could be cleaned up just a bit.</p>
<p>The journal is not a bad idea, but I didn’t feel like Marie was “alive”. I definitely feel bad for her, but the way she writes in her journal is almost robotic, mostly just listing off events that are happening. This is practical for the use of the article, but at the same time feels too convenient. I understand that this is a difficult balance to achieve, though.</p>
<p>The last interview to me felt almost completely unnecessary. While it helps to reiterate the guy’s intentions and his controlling nature, it also restates everything we already learned previously up to this point. The interviewer also seems out of character for the Foundation. They could most likely see what was going on in this toxic relationship without needing to ask him about it.</p>
<p>Now, for what I liked about it! I found it off the series page because the pink caught my eye, and the name combined with that was interesting. Initially, I thought it seemed very cute. Two lovers who can never be separated. But then I saw what was really going on, and my heart sank. That emotional reaction is what struck me the most about the article, because abusive relationships are so depressing.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<br />
Overall, I like it though. Upvoted. I hope you end up tweaking this more if you ever feel like it, because I’d love to see this be the best article it can be.
							</div>

								
					
